  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Concept: Overlapping of only same phase creates bonding.<br />(I) There is no case of bonding as a positive phase cannot simultaneously make bond with other orbital's positive as well as negative phase<br />(II) This creates bonding of p and d orbital.<br />(III) This creates bonding of two 'p' orbitals.<br />(IV) This is the case of anti-bonding of two 'd' orbitals.",
